    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Douglass returns for his adult preventive visit seven weeks after his five-month review. His voice recovered fully within ten days of the laryngitis in June. He writes most days with right-hand pain of about 2 of 10, using the diclofenac gel before long sessions and keeping up his hand exercises. He sleeps about seven hours on most nights and has had a nightmare about once a month. He does not drink and has never used tobacco. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit and agreed to each part of today&apos;s visit as it was explained. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit, age 34</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Post-traumatic osteoarthritis of the right hand, controlled; personal history of psychological trauma with symptoms below the threshold for PTSD; short sleep, improved</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Diclofenac 1% gel to the right hand as needed</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent; working full days, writing and traveling to speak</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Very good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Supported by his family, his community, and his church; work is demanding and purposeful</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>No alcohol (AUDIT-C 0), tobacco, or other drugs</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals; eats late on writing nights</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks most days, about 30 minutes; hand exercises daily</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in all</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours on most nights; a nightmare about once a month</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt; no firearms at home; smoke detectors working; plans his travel for talks with care because of past threats</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No concerns; visual acuity normal in each eye at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Married, one partner; no concerns</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

