    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. PHQ-2 0. AUDIT-C 0. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Post-traumatic osteoarthritis of the right hand (M19.141)</content>. Controlled; writing without limits most days. [S]<list><item>Continue the gel as needed and the home exercises.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Personal history of psychological trauma (Z91.49)</content>. Symptoms below the threshold for PTSD and improving; PCL-5 16 at the August review. [S]<list><item>PCL-5 and PHQ-9 at the next chronic-care review.</item><item>He may return to Dr. Morrison at any time.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, 1852-1853</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today, with his agreement</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, 1852-1853</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; he will get it at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap about five years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Three-dose series in infancy in his childhood record</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Once for all adults; drawn today with his agreement; the result will be sent to him</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Once for all adults; antibody drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Once for all adults with the three-test panel; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>120/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended for adults 35 to 70 with overweight or obesity; he is 34 with a BMI of 24.8</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 0</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never used</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Starts at 45; no family history known to him</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular risk and statin assessment</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Begins at 40; normal blood pressure, no diabetes, never smoked</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 1852-1853 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026); Screening and Testing for Hepatitis B Virus Infection: CDC Recommendations, United States, 2023 (2023)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: HIV, hepatitis C, and hepatitis B results by message. Chronic-care review in three to six months. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

